## HbTK

Installation and build instructions for HbTK.

## Requirements

HbTK requires:

```
C++ compiler
X11 development libraries
GNU Make
Autoconf
Automake
Libtool
```

## Building from a Source Archive

If the source archive already contains a generated `configure` script:

```
./configure --prefix=/usr
make -j$(nproc)
sudo make install
```

## Building from Git

When building directly from the Git source tree, regenerate the
Autotools build files first:

```
autoreconf -fi
```

Then configure and build:

```
./configure --prefix=/usr
make -j$(nproc)
sudo make install
```

## Configure Options

The installation prefix can be changed with `--prefix`:

```
./configure --prefix=/usr/local
```

The default prefix is:

```
/usr/local
```

## Cleaning

Remove compiled objects and other build output:

```
make clean
```

To completely regenerate the configured build:

```
make distclean
```

When rebuilding the Autotools files from Git:

```
autoreconf -fi
./configure --prefix=/usr
```

## Uninstall

If the generated Makefile supports uninstall:

```
sudo make uninstall
```

## Installation Files

HbTK installs its toolkit files according to the configured installation
prefix.

The exact installed files and locations may change while HbTK is being
developed.

## Documentation

Additional project documentation:

```
